{{ usage_hours | default("As agreed by the Parties.") }}

3.3 The Tenant/User shall permit reasonable access to the Landlord/Owner for inspection, repair and maintenance and shall comply with all applicable laws and fire and safety requirements.


4. TERM AND TERMINATION

4.1 This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and continue for the Term. Auto-renew is {{ auto_renew | default("No") }}.

4.2 Either Party may terminate this Agreement upon material breach that remains uncured for 14 days after written notice, or immediately upon the insolvency of the other Party.

4.3 The Tenant/User shall vacate the premises and deliver them in a clean and reasonable condition on expiry or termination, and shall return all keys and access devices.


5. LIABILITY AND INSURANCE

5.1 NEITHER PARTY SHALL BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES.

5.2 The Tenant/User shall maintain adequate insurance covering its obligations under this Agreement, and the Landlord/Owner shall maintain insurance appropriate to its ownership interest.


6. GOVERNING LAW AND DISPUTE RESOLUTION

6.1 This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of {{ governing_law | default("Sri Lanka") }}.

6.2 Any dispute arising out of or in connection with this Agreement shall be resolved by {{ dispute_resolution | default("Arbitration") }} in accordance with the chosen institution's rules, and the decision shall be final and binding on the Parties.

6.3 Where the Parties have agreed a registered tenancy, this Agreement is subject to the registration and any stamp duty or notarization requirements of the applicable jurisdiction.


7. GENERAL PROVISIONS

7.1 This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties and supersedes all prior understandings.

7.2 No amendment or waiver shall be binding unless in writing and signed by both Parties.

7.3 Notices shall be given in writing to the addresses first written above.


